# Poka-yoke and adversarial review

False PASS (incomplete kit marked complete / AUTO_PASS) is the red-line failure. Make the wrong action impossible; do not add a warning and continue.

## Poka-yoke (must remain true)

- No AUTO_PASS if caption inconsistent, MISSING nonempty, CONFIDENCE=LOW, UNCLEAR nonempty, or occlusion.
- Operator cannot “Gate was right” on HOLD (API 400 + UI disabled).
- Override requires a non-`agree` reason. AUTO_FAIL → COMPLETE needs a second confirm.
- Ingest: filename regex + known `kit_id` only; custom_prompt ≤800; no YouTube/http file paths.
- `scripts/push_both.sh` refuses clips/secrets and fails if origin or github push fails.

## Adversarial review (every change)

Before you commit: run attacks that should fail closed (false PASS, illegal operator POST, bad filename, 801-char prompt, YouTube path). Record them in `.cursor/adversarial/` with Attack / Expected / Result / Fix. If an attack succeeds, fix it before any other work. Happy-path tests alone are not enough.

Do not ask Bryce to invent these attacks; use the list in `.cursor/handoffs/chatgpt-cowork.md` and extend it when you add a surface.
